title: One renderer, desktop and browser
intro: Griff draws through one renderer now. Each frame becomes a draw list that OpenGL draws on the desktop and WebGL draws in the browser, so a dark scene's lights and shadows and the camera's screen effects look the same in both.
project: Empty | Same Pixels

chapter: The dark | Lights and shadows, from the draw list
create: Sprite
rename: Floor
set: Sprite.Size = 30, 20
set: Sprite.Tint = #8A8070
say: A floor the color of stone, so we can see where the light falls.
create: Light
rename: Lamp
set: Transform.Position = 0, 0, 0
set: Light.Radius = 8
set: Light.Shadows = true
expectvalue: Lamp.Light.Shadows = true
select: Floor
create: Sprite
rename: Wall
set: Transform.Position = 3, 0, 0
set: Sprite.Size = 0.6, 3
set: Sprite.Tint = #5F574F
add: BoxCollider
set: BoxCollider.Size = 0.6, 3
expectat: Lamp = 0, 0
expectat: Wall = 3, 0

select: Main Camera
set: Camera.Ambient = #202030
expectvalue: Main Camera.Camera.Ambient = #202030
say: A dark ambient light on the camera, a lamp that casts shadows, and a wall in its way.
play
wait: 1
expectdrawn: -3, 0 = lit
expectdrawn: 5, 0 = dark
explain: game | Drawn from a draw list | Every frame is turned into a draw list: its quads, already placed on the screen, and the passes that draw them. Here the floor and the wall, then a light map that starts at the ambient light, the lamp added up in it where its shadows don't reach, and the map laid over the floor.
say: The desktop runs those passes with OpenGL. The web player runs the very same list with WebGL, with the same shaders, so the browser now shows the dark, its lights and its shadows too.
stop

chapter: Screen effects | The same in the browser
select: Main Camera
add: ScreenEffects
set: ScreenEffects.Scanlines = 0.6
set: ScreenEffects.Curvature = 0.35
set: ScreenEffects.Palette = GameBoy
expectvalue: Main Camera.ScreenEffects.Palette = GameBoy
play
wait: 1
expectdrawn: -3, 0 = lit
expectdrawn: 5, 0 = #0F380F
explain: game | Screen effects | Screen effects are one more pass: the frame is drawn into a picture, and the picture onto the screen through the old TV and the handheld's four greens. In a browser they used to be left out. Now they're drawn there as here.
say: To keep it that way, a check draws every template, and scenes like this one, both ways, on the desktop and in a browser with no window, and compares the pictures pixel by pixel.
stop
